      "working_with_eating_disorders_requires": "Working with eating disorders requires emotional sustainability",
      "you_decoded_this_label_correctly_move_": "You decoded this label correctly. Move to the next challenge.",
      "you_don_t_have_to_wait_for_things_to_g": "You don't have to wait for things to get worse to ask for help. You don't have to \"earn\" support by being sick enough. You just have to reach out.",
      "you_don_t_need_to_know_what_to_say_the": "You don't need to know what to say. They're trained to start the conversation. You can call back. You can hang up. You can't do it wrong.",
      "you_don_t_owe_anyone_your_attention_re": "You don't owe anyone your attention. Removing harmful accounts is a self-care move, not rudeness.",
      "you_or_someone_you_love_can_come_throu": "You — or someone you love — can come through this.",
      "your_body_has_three_different_ways_to_": "Your body has three different ways to make ATP. They're all running constantly, but the dominant system depends on how hard and how long you're working.",
      "your_body_holds_only_50_g_of_atp_at_an": "Your body holds only ~50 g of ATP at any moment, but recycles it constantly: each ATP molecule cycles ATP → ADP → ATP about 1,000+ times per day. Total ATP turnover roughly equals your body weight per day. The recycling happens in tiny organelles called mitochondria, which use oxygen and food (glucose, fatty acids) to charge ADP back into ATP.",
      "your_body_needs_at_least_your_bmr_wort": "Your body needs at least your BMR worth of energy to keep its essential systems working. Eating well below BMR for an extended time forces the body to slow metabolism, break down muscle, weaken immunity, and impair concentration. The goal isn't to \"minimize calories\" — it's to give your body what it needs to do its job. If anything in this module triggers worry about how much you're eating, please talk with a trusted adult, your doctor, or NEDA (1-800-931-2237).",
