      "when_books_spread_fast_authorities_tri": "When books spread fast, authorities tried to control them. Imprimatur (license to print), 1559 Index of Forbidden Books, banned authors, samizdat smuggling. The 1500-year cat-and-mouse between print and power.",
      "when_leading_is_open_the_text_breathes": "When leading is open, the text breathes and the eye finds the next line easily.",
      "when_the_leading_is_too_tight_lines_of": "When the leading is too tight, lines of text feel cramped and the eye loses its place between them.",
      "when_the_right_edge_of_a_paragraph_is_": "When the right edge of a paragraph is allowed to fall where it falls, the result is called ragged-right. Each line ends with a natural word break.",
      "when_the_right_edge_of_a_paragraph_is__2": "When the right edge of a paragraph is forced to align, the compositor inserts thin metal spacers between words so every line ends at the same position.",
