      "rip_currents_are_narrow_after_30_100_f": " Rip currents are narrow. After 30-100 feet of parallel swimming you will be in normal water and can swim back to shore at an angle.",
      "rip_currents_pull_thousands_of_beachgo": "Rip currents pull thousands of beachgoers out to sea every year on US coasts, including Maine. The escape technique is counterintuitive — most people get it wrong because they panic.",
      "roll_away_do_not_stand": "Roll away. Do not stand. ",
      "rubbing_pushes_cold_blood_from_the_arm": "Rubbing pushes cold blood from the arms and legs back to the warming core. This \"afterdrop\" can cause cardiac arrest.",
